-- title:
--   One forward (DIF) transform pass over all levels of a Fermat-ring tensor
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a list of $N \le 2^{kb}$ canonical residues modulo $2^n+1$ on stack `XD`, and let $D$ be a list of level descriptors $(\mathrm{pre}, j, E, \mathrm{post})$ satisfying `LvlOK n kb W N J D` (each level splits the array into $\mathrm{pre}$ blocks of $2^j$ columns of length $\mathrm{post}$ with $\mathrm{pre}\cdot 2^j\cdot\mathrm{post}=N$, $2^j E = 2n$, $j\le J$), encoded as 8 integers per level (`enc8`) on the source stack. With $2n+kb+3 \le W$, $J+1\le W$, $\mathrm{zsz}(|D|)\le W$ and the registers holding $kb$, $N$, $2^n$, $2^n+1$, $|D|$, the program `passP` with the forward (DIF) butterfly procedure replaces $A$ by `lvls (Gd n = difZ (2^n+1)) D A` (the forward (DIF) radix-2 Fermat transform of every column of every level, applied level by level), moves the descriptor list to the other descriptor stack (reversed), within cost `passCost |D| n kb W N J`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** `difZ`/`ditZ` are the decimation-in-frequency / -time transforms with root $2$-power of the published `Def_IntMul_HvdH_MachineRef`; each column transform is a call of procedure 2 or 3. The machine layer: `IState HS` is a state with $64$ stacks of items (`Item` = integer or mark), an input position and an output; `RM` programs (straight-line register code `RS`, loops `rep`, conditionals, calls of the multiplication procedure through a `MulSpec` $M$ giving its domain and cost) have a functional semantics `p.run s`, a definedness predicate `p.ok M s` and a cost `p.cost M s`; `Spec M p s s' c` abbreviates `p.ok M s ∧ p.run s = s' ∧ p.cost M s ≤ c`. `ints L` / `gints U` push an integer list / a list of pairs as items (head = top); `zsz z` is the bit length of $|z|$. `MulBnd M m Φ` says the multiplication procedure accepts all pairs of integers of bit length $\le m$ at cost $\le Φ$. Register names (`GU`, `CR`, `KB`, `XN`, …) are fixed stack indices.
-- source:
--   D. Harvey, J. van der Hoeven, Integer multiplication in time O(n log n), Ann. of Math. 193 (2021), 563–617 (Theorem 1.1: multitape Turing machine multiplication in O(n log n)). Lemma `NLogN.FW.passF_spec` of the Lean development NLogN/HFW9.lean (lines 102–120), written for the prove2.me integer-multiplication campaign.

